# See it on a phone

People will read your book on phones, tablets and e-readers. The buttons above the preview show it at each size.

1. Click [Phone]{.ui}. The page narrows to the shape of a phone screen, and the text wraps to fit.
2. Click [E-reader]{.ui} to see the same page on a larger screen.
3. Use [Previous chapter]{.ui} and [Next chapter]{.ui} to move between your two chapters.
4. Click [Reader]{.ui} to try the controls a reading app gives your readers, such as a dark theme and larger text.

![The preview in the Phone view, with the chapter on a narrow page.](../Images/screen-phone.png){.figure .screenshot}

Click [Fill]{.ui} to go back to a preview that fills its half of the screen.

You do not lay out pages for each screen. Your text flows to fit whatever screen it is read on.
